{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A restart between the checkpoint and dispatch can leave the gate polling indefinitely for a workflow that was never started."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A restart after the handle is cleared but before the result is saved repeats the completed gate."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Cleanup can delete the branches and lose track of an active workflow, wasting runner time."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A temporary rate limit cancels and fails the gate, wasting the work already performed by the workflow."}]}